  "Q1": "Same admitted unbound lease veto before GetOrCreate closes observed bootstrap gap. Existing bound fence protects canonical recovery/writes and finalization, not unconditional callback/checkpoint non-entry.",
  "Q2": "Marker.G negative comparison only is acceptable. Never pass/return/cache/install it as binding or capability; equal claims must still pass ordinary real proof.",
  "Q3": "Keep existing storage admission/recovery order for quiescent observed contour. No new below-admission reader/quarantine/debt policy.",
  "Q4": "Mandatory fresh BOTH/discovery/catalog -> first actual Late2 -> independent EVIDENCE -> finite helper/wrapper/affected-consumer controls -> corrected G2 -> independent EVIDENCE before seven successors. Prior same-G/default scoped PASS may retain historical provenance after exact authored dependency equivalence; no unconditional cold/retained/newroot/newA rerun.",
  "mandatoryRefinements": [
    "Share only pure Parse/Matches/Tuple helpers; preserve existing hold identified state/catch body",
    "Private static early helper(files, lease) is sufficient; no public grant/API",
    "Propagate early read failure instead of NotApplicable bootstrap",
    "Preserve existing bound/expected/default/close behavior; do not claim pre-callback physical verification",
    "Three proposed wrapper cases alone do not cover helper applicability and G validation"
  ],
  "integrationSelectionRequirements": [
